Z||000019||Shaun41178||04-20-2001||10:43 AM||||Damn travis that is kickass.  Even cooler reading about how he came in to have it dynoed.  I guarantee he will be back for the supercharger kit.  Badass man.  Funny how he called the number.  318 at the wheels is impressive.  <P>Hey trav any new knews on that shaved intake?  get it dynoed?<P>All Fiero owners should get to <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000020||1FST2M6||04-20-2001||10:48 AM||||i'll scan these dyno sheets  we had to gring the valve covers.. the bottom of the middle intake was droped .4" and that interfeeried with the wiring harness and the valve cover.. it picked up 6hp at 3800rpm and caried it through the rest of the gear.. but i lost 8lbft off idle and to 3000rpm||||reg||1
Z||000021||Shaun41178||04-20-2001||11:53 AM||||Oh so you did end up grinding the bottom of the lower intake huh?  So you took some off the bottom of the middle, the top of the middle, and the bottom of the top?  How much total then?<P>The bottom of the middle still lined up good with the top of the lower?<P>6hp is pretty good.  Torque loss is bad but I was expecting that.<P>You want to grind down the intake you took off your car and perhaps swap them on mine if and when I head up there to put my heads on?  Maybe only take like .2 off he bottom of the middle?  It will all be off anyways.  i could use an extra 6 hp more  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Later man<BR> <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000022||lou_dias||04-20-2001||12:37 PM||||So does this combination work well with the big bore throttle body?<P>Trav:  What effect does the bigger throttle body have on a stock 2.8, I just picked up an 88GT since my 3.5L 87GT beast died on me last month.<P>Now that I have an extra GT, I can send out the 87 TB and when it comes back, put it on the 88...right...?<P>Anybody have the "Holley" or clone scoop for sale?||||reg||1
Z||000023||1FST2M6||04-20-2001||02:07 PM||||tigger has a sharp intake scoop.. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstintake1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstintake1.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstintake2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstintake2.jpg</A>  <P>all total the intake lost 1.37" and it was REALLLLLY close to the fuel pressure regulator! ed is working on a spare fuel rail i had and seeing if we can loose the stock FPR and install just the Stillen or Vortech units and see if we can't gain more clearance. and more hp.. but we REALLY need to figure out how to get the torque back.. nitrous will work..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> more results to come.. and the TB question Lou.. uum Shaun dynoed it and it didn't make much of a difference on his car..  (V6-Auto)i'm still running the stock TB... for now... a pair may be in my future...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||Shaun41178||04-20-2001||02:29 PM||||I picked up 4 peak hp and around 3 lb ft of torque with just the addition of the ported TB by darrel morse.  THe dyno graph was put up on this forum a while back.<P>There was also an increase throughout the entire rpm band.  it didn't lose any power that is for sure.  A matched intake plenum will give even better results.  <P>ported TB was dyno tested on my internally stock 2.8 with about 50k or so on it.<P>What happened to your 3.5L Lou?  And yes you can send it out and put it on your 88.  there are no differences between the years<P>Trav I was thinking of getting a adj FPR from Summit.  The one with the little dial on the top so it can be turned by hand.  I wonder if that one sits higher then the stock one.?<P>a pair of TB would be kick@ss.  Any news from Chris about that setup yet?<BR> <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <BR>||||reg||1
